import ObsmetrologiaManual.DocSetup

open Verso.Genre Manual InlineLean

/-!
Style rules for writing Obsmetrologia documentation.
-/

#doc (Manual) "Documentation style" =>

# Documentation Style

Obsmetrologia documentation should be calm, explicit, and mathematically hospitable.
It can be ambitious without becoming mystical, and formal without becoming
opaque.

## Preferred Moves

Say "generated by" when generation matters.

Say "recovered as" when a familiar mathematical object appears later in the
chain.

Say "frontier" when the claim is exploratory.

Say "not yet formalized" when prose outruns Lean.

Say "witnessed by" when a Lean declaration, finite certificate, or checked
example supports the prose.

## Avoid

Avoid presenting analogies as definitions.

Avoid replacing Obsmetrologia terms with familiar textbook terms too early.

Avoid status ambiguity. A reader should be able to tell whether a passage is
normative foundation, recovered mathematics, frontier exploration, or provenance.

Avoid documentation that only describes files. Explain the mathematical role of
the files.

## Status Language

Use stable status labels:

* normative,
* recovered,
* frontier,
* conjectural,
* computational witness,
* prose only,
* Lean checked,
* archived.

Status labels should be boring on purpose. The mathematics can be strange; the
metadata should not be.

## Examples

Examples should be small enough to read and faithful enough to matter. A checked
example is better than a grand unverified illustration. A frontier example is
fine when it is marked as frontier.
